{"type":"standard","title":"Laurel Lee","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Laurel Lee</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q61483038","titles":{"canonical":"Laurel_Lee","normalized":"Laurel Lee","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Laurel Lee</span></span>"},"pageid":59796805,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Laurel_Lee_118thCong.jpeg/330px-Laurel_Lee_118thCong.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/77/Laurel_Lee_118thCong.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":3360,"height":4200},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1368849646","tid":"2afefcfb-957d-11f1-b693-05264b203b83","timestamp":"2026-08-11T12:07:05Z","description":"American judge and politician (born 1974)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurel_Lee","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurel_Lee?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurel_Lee?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Laurel_Lee"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurel_Lee","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Laurel_Lee","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurel_Lee?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Laurel_Lee"}},"extract":"Laurel Frances Lee is an American attorney, former judge, and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Florida's 15th congressional district since 2023. A member of the Republican Party, she previously served as Florida's secretary of state from 2019 to 2022 and as a judge on Florida's Thirteenth Judicial Circuit from 2013 to 2019.","extract_html":"<p><b>Laurel Frances Lee</b> is an American attorney, former judge, and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Florida's 15th congressional district since 2023. A member of the Republican Party, she previously served as Florida's secretary of state from 2019 to 2022 and as a judge on Florida's Thirteenth Judicial Circuit from 2013 to 2019.</p>"}